# Memory Refactor Roadmap and Progress

This rule tracks the ongoing architectural refactor from vision-only to memory-based arenas, including a hybrid VISION mode that uses instant, memory-based resets. Update this file at the end of each feature sprint or major change.

## What exists now (scaffolding in place)
- Memory-mode environment: [EldenMemoryEnv.py](mdc:EldenMemoryEnv.py)
  - Observations are numeric (hp, stamina, boss hp, time alive, phase)
  - Resets use memory-based instant teleport/restore via [MemoryClient.py](mdc:MemoryClient.py)
  - Shares input execution with vision via [InputController.py](mdc:InputController.py)
- Reward for memory mode: [EldenRewardMemory.py](mdc:EldenRewardMemory.py)
  - Reward logic uses precise values from memory reads
- YAML-driven arena config (loaded by default):
  - Sample config: [config/memory_arenas.sample.yaml](mdc:config/memory_arenas.sample.yaml)
  - Load order (first found): `MEMORY_CONFIG_PATH` → `config/memory_arenas.yaml` → sample
  - Defaults wired in [main.py](mdc:main.py); also used by [EldenMemoryEnv.py](mdc:EldenMemoryEnv.py) → [MemoryClient.py](mdc:MemoryClient.py)
- Hybrid VISION mode resets (instant): [EldenEnv.py](mdc:EldenEnv.py)
  - Uses memory-based arena reset; retains vision observations/reward
- Shared input system: [InputController.py](mdc:InputController.py)
- Training unchanged: [train.py](mdc:train.py)
- Updated documentation: [README.md](mdc:README.md)

Notes:
- `walkToBoss.py` is not used anymore by default. Keep or delete depending on legacy needs.

## What’s left (high-level backlogs)
1) Memory backend (core)
   - Implement real process attach/handle management
   - Implement reliable read/write for player hp/stamina, boss hp, player pos, boss state/flags
   - Error handling, safety checks, and offline/single-player guarantees
2) Signature scanning & offsets
   - Add a SignatureScanner to find addresses across game versions
   - Maintain an OffsetDB for known versions; fallback to signature scan
3) Arena coverage
   - Fill YAML per-boss: spawn coords, camera, second phase triggers, flags
   - Implement boss reset semantics (fog gates, AI state neutralization)
   - Validate boundaries and soft-lock prevention
4) Observation space extensions (optional)
   - Add exact positions/velocities/orientations if needed by policies
5) Performance & stability
   - Optimize read frequency and caching
   - Optional threading for memory polling
6) Testing & validation
   - Add unit tests for MemoryClient read/write adapters
   - Add integration tests for reset sequences
   - Version compatibility checks and graceful degradation
7) Tooling & DX
   - CLI utilities to dump/verify addresses
   - Logging/telemetry of memory ops for debugging

## Near-term milestones
- M1: Real memory read/write for hp, stamina, boss hp, and player position
  - DoD: Deterministic hp/stamina reads; reliable teleport; boss hp reset
- M2: First arena end-to-end (e.g., Beastman, farmum azula)
  - DoD: From reset() → spawn in arena → fight steps → death/boss kill → reset() works repeatedly
- M3: Safety/compat
  - DoD: Check offline mode; add basic anti-cheat-safe toggles; basic version gating
- M4: Signature scanning prototype
  - DoD: Resolve at least player hp address via signature; store in OffsetDB

## Config defaults
- `ENV_MODE`: VISION or MEMORY
- `RESET_MODE`: MEMORY (default for VISION env to use instant resets)
- `PROCESS_NAME`: defaults to `eldenring.exe`
- YAML load order: `MEMORY_CONFIG_PATH` → `config/memory_arenas.yaml` → `config/memory_arenas.sample.yaml`

## Update cadence
- After each feature sprint/major change, update:
  - “What exists now” with new modules/behaviors
  - Backlogs and milestones (mark delivered/adjust next steps)

